{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"xamarin.forms platform projects xamarin.forms platform projects","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md","fileName":"Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cross-Platform .NET Mobile Runtime]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cross-Platform .NET Mobile Runtime","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"xamarin.forms platform projects xamarin.forms platform projects","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md","fileName":"Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects","heading":"Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A Xamarin.Forms solution contains shared application code alongside platform projects for Android and iOS. Each platform project supplies the native entry point, application metadata, resources, permissions, and any platform-specific implementations.\n\nThis structure concentrates reusable pages and domain logic while retaining access to native behavior where required. Build and release testing must still cover every platform because packaging and operating-system integration are not shared in the same way as C# logic.\n\nThe book's solution keeps shared Xamarin.Forms code in one project and Android-specific permissions, manifest entries, resources, and plugin initialization in the Android project. An iOS target would add its own platform project while referencing the same shared application.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cross-Platform .NET Mobile Runtime","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"xamarin.forms platform projects xamarin.forms platform projects","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md","fileName":"Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Xamarin.Forms Platform Projects","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cross-Platform .NET Mobile Runtime","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}